    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7330" root="حدث" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْدَثٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَدِيثٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَدَثٌ</span>,
in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, applied to a poet, <i>i. q.</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَلَّدٌ</span> [<i>A post-classical author:</i> itself a post-classical term]. (Mz 49th <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نوع</span>.) [And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُحْدَثُونَ</span>
<i>The moderns;</i> or <i>people of later times;</i> opposed
to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القُدَمَآءُ</span>.]

